Draw_Car / FUN_0042c2d4: contiguous 9-short light matrix (scattered-locals)

gte_MulMatrix0 writes a 9-short (0x12-byte) matrix through its out arg (asm: lea eax,[ebp-0x2c]
in Draw_Car @0x42c15c, [ebp-0x30] in FUN_0042c2d4 @0x42c2d4). Ghidra declared only the first
three shorts (sStack_30/local_2e/sStack_2c resp. sStack_34/local_32/sStack_30) -- the three the
function then rescales -- and __lmptr = &first is handed to the rasterizer which reads all NINE.
The compiler does not lay scattered locals contiguously, so 6 of 9 lanes were garbage/UB.
